# Logs
*.log
# DEBUG_JSON forensic logs (agent/app.py) — already covered by *.log above,
# named explicitly since they can contain planted payloads / doc splices /
# demo sink strings and must never be committed. Split by direction/endpoint:
# tx_llm (outbound to LLM), rx_llm (inbound from LLM), tx_mcp (MCP tool call),
# rx_mcp (MCP tool result). The trailing "*" also covers rotated backups
# (e.g. tx_llm.log.1), which *.log alone would not match.
agent/tx_llm.log*
agent/rx_llm.log*
agent/tx_mcp.log*
agent/rx_mcp.log*

# OWASP test-harness tool-invocation log — same sensitivity as debug_json.log
# above (planted payloads, simulated PII/secrets). *.log already covers the
# file itself; the directory is named explicitly for clarity.
test_harness/logs/
# sweep.py output — full replies, so the same leaked canary PII/secrets.
test_harness/sweep*.jsonl
test_harness/sweep*.txt

# Internal ops runbook — real VM users/paths/SSH-key names, not for the
# public repo. Kept locally for reference; untracked via `git rm --cached`.
